{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xtknbhh6botq46egrq2s4l3nryyc3kou5y5sit3t3lsnhxvuayaa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — **all four phases pass, and the Rust translation needed no fixes** (the divergences I found were all in my own test harness, which I corrected).\n\n## Results\n\n**Phase A — surface mapped**\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — C `.so` exports **16** symbols, Rust `.so` exports the **same 16**; `comm` diff empty both ways; all undefined symbols are libc/unwinder imports. Assertion expression strings, `__PRETTY_FUNCTION__` names and line numbers baked into both binaries are byte-identical.\n- `ERRORS.md` — **94 rows**, one per distinct rejection grepped out of `lib.c` (sentinel returns, all 9 `assert()`s, every `switch` default, every min/max constant, plus generic FFI boundaries).\n- `CONFIGS.md` — **78 rows**, the pruned cross-product of the axes the C actually branches on (`mode`, `string.mode`, seed, `elemsize`/`keysize`/`keyoffset`, grow/shrink/tombstone thresholds, arena block sizes, all 16 entry points including the lowest-level ones).\n\n**Phase B/C — 169 differential tests, all passing.** Both `.so`s are loaded via `libloading`; the Rust crate is never linked in. After *every* operation both libraries' full state is snapshot-compared: header, all `stbds_hash_index` fields, **every** bucket `hash[]`/`index[]` slot, and **every** element byte. `str_dups` is compared by capturing its `printf` bytes. Crash rows re-exec the test binary per library and compare **signal + exit code + normalised `assert()` text** — never \"both failed somehow\".\n\n**Phase D — completion gate.** `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` and `CMakeLists.txt` has no options, so the power set is one combination; `check_features.sh` derives that mechanically rather than assuming it and runs check/build/symbols/tests for each element. The suite additionally passes against the **dev-profile** `.so` (overflow-checks on), proving no arithmetic overflows where the C wraps.\n\n**Mutation-tested the suite** to prove it isn't vacuous — five deliberate \"fixes\" to C quirks were all caught, e.g. adding the `stbds_temp_key` write the C's wrap-around duplicate branch omits (caught), relaxing `hmdel_key`'s exact `mode == 1` to `>=` (30 tests fail), removing the `int` sign-extension in siphash (6 tests fail), and `slot_count <= 8` → `<` (39 tests fail).\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n- **`__FILE__` in assert messages cannot match**: the C `.so` embeds the absolute cmake path, the Rust hardcodes `src/lib.c`. This is a property of *where the C was compiled*, so the tests compare line/function/expression/signal and ignore the directory prefix (documented in `ERRORS.md` note (F)).\n- Some C paths are genuinely fatal and are verified as *crash-equivalent* rather than value-equivalent — notably a string lookup on a table whose `string.mode` falls into the `memcpy` branch, which dereferences key text as a pointer.\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `tests/{harness,configs,maps,errors}`, and `run_tests.sh` / `check_symbols.sh` / `check_features.sh` / `check_rows.sh`. Nothing under `c_src/` was modified (source md5s unchanged; only `c_src/build/` was created)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":946,"cache_read_input_tokens":351786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":946,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0f99972-4265-4275-9682-9ed22be120aa","uuid":"4865a0ee-e8f8-4c0a-bf54-7291411edb2c","timestamp":"2026-08-20T16:27:54.231Z"}
